# Variables are stored encrypted in secrets.vault.json (Ansible Vault).
#
# First-time setup (creates passphrase, cluster SSH key, encrypted vars):
#   make vault-setup
#
# Day-to-day:
#   make plan
#   make apply
#   make secrets-edit         # edit secrets.vault.json with $EDITOR
#   make secrets-view         # print decrypted JSON to stdout
#   make ssh-export           # restore .cluster_ssh/cluster_ed25519 on a new machine
#
# Sharing with a teammate: send them the vault passphrase via 1Password / Bitwarden.
# They clone the repo, write the passphrase to .vault_pass (mode 600), and run `make plan`.
